; ===========================================================================
; RADIATION TUNER (internal object, never given to the player).
;
; Why it exists: in this build RegisterScriptCallback("update", ...) never
; reaches our handlers (the callback registry is a local table inside
; dynamic_callbacks.lua and the Lua VM is recreated on init). But every game
; object with a script_binding gets its Lua update() called by the SCHEDULER
; every frame:
;   CGameObject::shedule_Update (GameObject.cpp:811-826)
;     -> CScriptBinder::shedule_Update (:825)
;       -> luabind::call_member<void>(this, "update", delta)
; The belt radiation uses the very same scheduler (CActor::shedule_Update,
; Actor.cpp:2013 -> UpdateArtefactsOnBeltAndOutfit at :2236).
;
; space_restrictor is the right base: class SPC_RS_S (a SERVER class, so it is
; created with alife():create), it has $spawn (so a client object exists and
; gets scheduled) and its script_binding slot is free - see system.ltx:621-626.
; No visual is needed: the object is invisible and harmless.
;
; The script spawns it next to the actor and removes the old one, so tuners do
; not pile up. On level change the engine destroys level objects by itself.
;
; inv_grid_width/height = 0 keep it out of the debug spawner: the spawner calls
; a section fake when both are present and <= 0 (SpawnManager.cpp:160-161).
; cost and inv_weight keep it out of the "unsorted" fakes list.
; ===========================================================================
[bq_rad_tuner]:space_restrictor
